// Plain-English understanding for Fort Bragg Local search.
//
// Each intent maps everyday words and phrases people actually type ("fix my sink",
// "teeth cleaning", "oil change", "kid doctor") to the kinds of businesses that help.
//   label  shown to the visitor: "Showing Plumbers"
//   p      phrases that trigger the intent (lowercase; plurals are handled automatically)
//   c      category ids. With no `s`, every business in these categories matches.
//   s      text that must appear in a business's type/tags (within `c` if given)
//   w      category ids the intent stays within, without matching all of them ("thai" finds Thai
//          restaurants, not Thai massage)
//   t      extra words that also match when found in a business's name, type or tags
//   r      the intent to show instead when the thing needs fixing ("fix my car" -> Car repair)
//   a      more ways to say it, understood in searches but not offered while typing ("my knee hurts")
//
// Keep phrases specific enough that they don't hijack business names. Single common
// words that are also business names (e.g. "union") must not be listed here.

// Where food is sold. Cuisines and dishes stay within these, so "chinese" isn't Chinese medicine.
